{"id":"svc-liability-cap","question":"What is the cap on each party's total aggregate liability?","reference_answer":"Liability is capped at the total fees paid or payable by the client under the applicable statement of work during the twelve (12) months preceding the claim.","answerable":true,"document":"service_agreement","relevant_clause_types":["liability"],"relevant_keywords":["total aggregate liability arising out of or related to this Agreement shall not exceed the total fees paid"],"gold_passages":["Except as set out in Section 6.1, each Party's total aggregate liability arising out of or related to this Agreement shall not exceed the total fees paid or payable by Client under the applicable Statement of Work during the twelve (12) months preceding the event giving rise to the claim."],"category":"qa"}
