{"id":"svc-renewal-notice","question":"What notice period is required to prevent automatic renewal?","reference_answer":"Either party must give written notice of non-renewal at least ninety (90) days before the end of the then-current term.","answerable":true,"document":"service_agreement","relevant_clause_types":["deadline","termination"],"relevant_keywords":["written notice of non-renewal at least ninety (90) days before the end of the then-current term"],"gold_passages":["This Agreement commences on the Effective Date and continues for an initial term of three (3) years (the \"Initial Term\"), renewing automatically for successive one (1) year periods unless either Party gives written notice of non-renewal at least ninety (90) days before the end of the then-current term."],"category":"qa"}
{"id":"svc-deliverable-acceptance","question":"How long does the client have to accept or reject a deliverable?","reference_answer":"The client must accept or reject each deliverable in writing within ten (10) business days of receipt; silence is deemed acceptance.","answerable":true,"document":"service_agreement","relevant_clause_types":["deadline","obligation"],"relevant_keywords":["accept or reject each deliverable in writing within ten (10) business days of receipt"],"gold_passages":["Client shall review and either accept or reject each deliverable in writing within ten (10) business days of receipt. Failure to respond within that period shall be deemed acceptance of the deliverable."],"category":"qa"}
